  "raw": {
    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497383/pro-se-prisoner-attorney-federal-pro-se-legal-assistance-program": {
      "title": "Pro Se Prisoner Attorney, Federal Pro Se Legal Assistance Program",
      "description": "Pro Se Prisoner Attorney, Federal Pro Se Legal Assistance Program Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497383 Type: Full-time Campus: North Haven - North Haven, CT Categories: Staff, Faculty Overview: Quinnipiac University’s School of Law invites applications for the Pro Se Prisoner Attorney for the Federal Pro Se Legal Assistance Program. The ideal candidate will advance Quinnipiac University School of Law's commitment to access to justice by providing legal assistance and guidance to incarcerated self-represented litigants with civil cases pending before the United States District Court for the District of Connecticut. The attorney will assist litigants in understanding court procedures, evaluating legal issues, responding to court orders, and navigating the federal litigation process, while helping to develop resources and systems that improve access to legal information and support. About the School: The Quinnipiac University School of Law is a student-centered law school with an outstanding and accessible teaching faculty, a 6:1 student-to-faculty ratio, an impressive range of externship and clinical opportunities, and a focus on collaboration and mentoring. The law school resides in a state-of-the-art facility on the university’s North Haven Campus, with a dynamic community of advanced programs including Quinnipiac’s School of Medicine. Quinnipiac Law enrolls almost 400 students pursuing a juris doctor degree or one of six joint degrees (combined degrees with other disciplines), including the JD/MBA. The law school offers concentrations in civil advocacy and dispute resolution; criminal law and advocacy; cybersecurity and information privacy; family law; health law; intellectual property; international law and policy; tax law; and workplace law. The School of Law is deeply committed to student success, bar passage, and career outcomes, and has made targeted investments in academic excellence, experiential learning, and curricular innovation, including expanded integration of skills-based and doctrinal instruction. Quinnipiac is fully approved by the American Bar Association and is a member of the Association of American Law Schools. For more information, please visit law.qu.edu. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 20 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles — including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men’s ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: Providing legal information, guidance, and assistance to incarcerated self-represented litigants with civil cases pending before the United States District Court for the District of Connecticut Explaining legal concepts and procedural requirements to litigants, including jurisdiction, venue, exhaustion of administrative remedies, and applicable court rules Assisting litigants with the preparation and amendment of pleadings, particularly following Initial Review Orders Responding to litigant inquiries regarding substantive and procedural aspects of federal civil litigation, with a primary focus on matters arising during the initial stages of a case Reviewing and explaining court orders, motions, pleadings, discovery obligations, and applicable federal and local rules Developing forms, instructional materials, and other resources to assist incarcerated self-represented litigants in navigating the litigation process Conducting in-person, telephonic, and virtual meetings with litigants and other stakeholders, as appropriate Maintaining case records and preparing written reports, summaries, and other documentation as required Supervising law student interns and externs Coordinating and collaborating with court personnel, law school personnel, legal services organizations, and community partners Identifying and facilitating referrals to appropriate courts, agencies, legal services providers, and community resources Assisting with program assessment, data collection, and other activities related to the evaluation and ongoing development of the Federal Pro Se Legal Assistance Program Other duties as assigned Education Requirements: Juris Doctor required Admitted to the Connecticut Bar, or eligible for admission; admission to or eligibility for admission to the United States District Court for the District of Connecticut preferred. Prior federal clerkship experience preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated knowledge of federal civil procedure and federal court practice, particularly in matters involving self-represented litigants Demonstrated ability to communicate clearly, professionally, and effectively with diverse audiences, including students, alumni, employers, faculty, staff, and members of the legal community. Skilled in delivering presentations and facilitating group discussions Excellent writing and editing skills, with the ability to prepare clear, concise, professional correspondence, reports, presentations, and other written materials for a variety of audiences Ability to analyze information, identify issues and opportunities, evaluate alternatives, and exercise sound judgment in developing practical and effective solutions Demonstrated commitment to providing responsive, respectful, and solutions-oriented service to students, alumni, employers, faculty, staff, and other law school constituents while adhering to University policies and procedures Ability to think creatively, generate new ideas, identify opportunities for improvement, and develop innovative approaches to programs, services, and workplace challenges Highly organized with the ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities, manage competing deadlines, coordinate projects, and maintain effective systems for tracking tasks and follow-up Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, roles, and professional settings. Ability to work collaboratively and independently Strong attention to detail and accuracy, with the ability to identify errors, maintain organized records, and ensure that projects, communications, and tasks are completed thoroughly and accurately Demonstrated ability to create a welcoming and respectful environment in which individuals from diverse backgrounds, perspectives, identities, and experiences feel valued and a sense of belonging. Ability to build positive relationships and work effectively with a wide range of individuals Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically and include a CV/resume, a cover letter detailing how your experience aligns with the position requirements, and contact information for three references. The anticipated salary range for this position is $90,000–$110,000. At the time of offer, the final salary will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications, including relevant education, experience, skills, and competencies, as well as internal equity and market considerations. Quinnipiac University offers eligible full-time faculty and staff a comprehensive benefits package that may include health insurance, life insurance, paid time off, education benefits, and retirement benefits. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where individuals feel valued, supported, and experience a strong sense of belonging. Advertised: October 09, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497407/parttime-faculty-mechanical-engineering-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty: Mechanical Engineering - Spring 2027",
      "description": "Part-Time Faculty: Mechanical Engineering - Spring 2027 Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497407 Type: Part-time Campus: Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: The School of Computing and Engineering at Quinnipiac University seeks highly qualified applicants who are committed to excellence in teaching for part-time faculty openings in Mechanical Engineering for the Spring 2027 semester and beyond. The school is looking to hire part-time faculty for the spring semester as well as maintain a pool of candidates should additional part-time openings arise. About the School/Program: The School of Computing and Engineering offers undergraduate degrees in civil, industrial, mechanical and software engineering, as well as AI & computing and computer science. It also offers graduate degrees in computer science, cybersecurity, and informatics. Dedicated to providing a first-rate engineering learning experience for our students, the school focuses on high-quality instruction, and offers hands-on training, applied learning opportunities and meaningful student-faculty relationships. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 20 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles — including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men’s ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: You will be responsible for all duties normally associated with teaching as a university faculty member, including but not limited to: Implementing common course syllabus, or developing and/or updating course syllabus, as applicable. Posting the syllabus to Canvas. Preparation of lectures, project, or other student assignments. Presenting instruction based on the competencies and performance levels of the course. Meeting all scheduled classes at the times published in the course schedule. Notifying your department chair or program director in advance and arranging for coverage, in the unusual event that you cannot be present at a scheduled class. Checking Quinnipiac email frequently to stay current with all communications. (This includes checking email for the five business days after the final grade submission deadline in the event a student appeals their final grade in your course(s) as permitted by the Procedure to Appeal a Final Grade in the Catalog.) Completing mandatory training within the time frame identified as defined by Human Resources. Examples include: Harassment & Discrimination, Data Security & Privacy and Managing Bias. The current spring semester openings are in day and early evening on-ground sections (some flexibility regarding offering time is possible) for the following courses: MER 340 – Manufacturing/Machine Design (3 credit) – This course introduces machine component design and manufacturing, relating fundamental engineering science to machine components. It covers load, stress and strain analyses, and fatigue . The course progresses to the study of machine component design, including mechanical components such as linkages, fasteners, springs, bearings, gears and shafts. MER 320 – Thermodynamics (3 credits) – This course focuses on thermodynamics. It applies conservation principles for mass, energy and linear momentum as well as the second law of thermodynamics. Principles are applied to power generation systems, refrigeration cycles and total air conditioning. Thermodynamic principles also are applied to the automotive system to examine engine performance (Otto and Diesel cycles) and to high performance aircraft to examine the Brayton cycle. MER 330L – Introduction to Circuits Lab (1 credit) - Students learn and practice hands-on techniques relevant to circuit analysis, such as bread board prototyping, voltage and current measurements, soldering, and basic data acquisition. All experimental results obtained in the lab are analyzed in the context of the theoretical framework presented in the course. Additional openings for the spring semester and beyond include foundation mechanical engineering course that include (but are not limited to) the following course offerings: MER 210 (Engineering Mechanics/Statics) MER 220 and MER 220L (Mechanics of Materials) MER 310 (Fluid Mechanics) Additional course and curriculum information may be found at Department of Mechanical and Industrial Engineering – Quinnipiac University Academic Catalog Education Requirements: A minimum of a Master’s degree in Engineering or a related field is preferred, although consideration will be given to excellent candidates who possess practical experience or professional licensure. Qualifications: Ability to teach assigned courses. Teaching experience at the undergraduate level. Proven ability to collaborate effectively with individuals from varied backgrounds. Special Instructions to Applicants: Quinnipiac University is considering only those applicants who have valid authorization to work in the United States. Quinnipiac University does not sponsor employment based visas for this position. TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter indicating your interest and qualification for the position, which course(s) you are interested in teaching, your teaching availability in terms of days of the week and times for the semester, and a curriculum vitae or resume including details of teaching experience. Consideration of candidates will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where individuals feel valued, supported, and experience a strong sense of belonging. Advertised: October 07, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497370/fulltime-clinical-faculty-school-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Full-Time Clinical Faculty: School of Nursing",
      "description": "Full-Time Clinical Faculty: School of Nursing Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497370 Type: Full-time Campus: North Haven - North Haven, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: Quinnipiac University's School of Nursing invites applicants who are dynamic educators and clinicians for a full-time, 12-month clinical track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. We are particularly interested in doctorally-prepared candidates with clinical practice and teaching experiences teaching across the lifespan with prelicensure BSN students. The position supports the School’s competency-based curriculum aligned with the AACN 2026 Essentials, emphasizing learner-centered approaches, clinical judgment, and integration of evidence-based practice. Faculty members in the School of Nursing contribute to the development of practice ready nurses through innovative teaching strategies and mentoring. Successful candidates will have experience teaching concepts such as person-centered care, population health, interprofessional practice, scholarship and inquiry, and informatics and healthcare technology with patients across the lifespan. Successful candidates are also able to contribute to the university’s strategic initiatives including empowering academic success, cultivating a community of learners, leading through innovation, designing distinctive experiences, redefining health and human potential, and extending our partnership. About the School/Program: The Quinnipiac University (QU) School of Nursing has been educating nurses for more than 50 years. Our mission is to develop exceptional, practice-ready nurses as leaders in science-based, holistic care through innovation and inclusive education. The School of Nursing was recently designated as a National League for Nursing (NLN) Center of Excellence. The School of Nursing’s strategic priorities are aligned with innovative programs, student success, thriving community, and sustainable resources. The School of Nursing serves approximately 1200 graduate and undergraduate students. We offer CCNE accredited programs leading to BSN, MSN, and DNP degrees that prepare graduates for successful careers in hospitals, clinics, schools, communities, and many other settings. The QU School of Nursing partners with Hartford HealthCare (HHC) with a New Careers in Nursing (NCN) work-compatible program for mid-career professionals interested in a future nursing career. As one of 17 schools in the nation with holistically endorsed programs, we emphasize the social, emotional, spiritual, and psychological aspects of care, as well as the physical, throughout our nursing curriculum. School of Nursing graduates become leaders at each level of their careers and facilitate positive changes within healthcare. Faculty and staff work with colleagues in our Center for Medicine, Nursing and Health Sciences and all schools across campus to create innovative interprofessional educational experiences that prepare students for today's health care challenges. The Center is located at our North Haven, CT campus and encompasses 325,000 square feet designed for collaborative learning including 48 pro-section stations, 16 standardized patient rooms, an exceptional health sciences library, 7 high-fidelity simulation rooms including 2 ORs and a PACU, health assessment and skills labs, advanced diagnostic imaging equipment and classrooms outfitted with the latest technology. The NCN Program is offered at the Center for Education, Simulation and Innovation (CESI) at Hartford HealthCare. We are a highly collaborative and supportive community that is committed to high quality educational experience, advancing diversity in all areas. Successful candidates will share the School of Nursing values of belonging, compassion, collaboration, curiosity, and integrity. The School provides faculty members with: A structured orientation and mentoring An assigned faculty affiliate Regular workshops by Quinnipiac Innovations in Learning and Teaching (QILT) Opportunities to work with nationally recognized faculty and staff Generous support for conference attendance and professional development Support with grant applications for faculty research or curricular innovations A culture of community, teamwork, and professionalism A climate that values diversity and inclusion Values of belonging, collaboration, compassion, curiosity and integrity Faculty are provided with one day a week as a practice and/or scholarship day. On-ground in person presence is expected on the campus 3 days per week. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 20 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles — including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men’s ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: Teaching intensive, clinical track nursing faculty position, with primary responsibility teaching in the New Careers in Nursing (NCN) work compatible program for mid-career professionals transitioning into nursing at the Center for Education, Simulation and Innovation (CESI) at Hartford HealthCare in Hartford, CT; faculty will also have teaching responsibilities on the North Haven campus Collaborate with colleagues to ensure high-quality programs that demonstrate academic excellence and success Participate in competency-based curriculum development, assessment, and continuous quality improvement aligned with the AACN 2026 Essentials Advise and mentor students to support academic success and professional growth Contribute to School and University service, including committee participation and professional engagement within the community Engage in scholarly activities and maintain currency in nursing practice and education Participate in faculty development Engage in the School of Nursing’s strategic plan Actively participate in the School of Nursing community Education Requirements: Required: unencumbered RN license in Connecticut Required: doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DNP) in nursing or related field Qualifications: Recent clinical practice experience Experience with competency-based education and curriculum development Evidence of effective teaching Service to profession or community Commitment to contribute to the excellence of the academic community Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically and include a resume, a cover letter detailing how your experience aligns with the position requirements, demonstrated commitment to intentional leadership that values individuals of all backgrounds and experiences, and contact information for three references. We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes tuition remission and a culture that is inclusive and driven by excellence. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful community. Advertised: September 17, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497155/fulltime-clinical-faculty-program-director-school-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Full-Time Clinical Faculty Program Director: School of Nursing",
      "description": "Full-Time Clinical Faculty Program Director: School of Nursing Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497155 Type: Full-time Campus: North Haven - North Haven, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: Quinnipiac University's School of Nursing invites applicants who are dynamic psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner (PMHNP) clinicians and educators for a full-time, 12-month clinical track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor to serve as Program Director for the PMHNP program. We are particularly interested in doctorally-prepared candidates with practice, teaching, and leadership experiences in a PMHNP graduate program. The position supports the School’s competency-based curriculum aligned with the AACN 2021 Essentials, emphasizing learner-centered approaches, clinical judgment, and integration of evidence-based practice. Faculty members in the School of Nursing contribute to the development of practice ready nurses and advanced practice nurses through innovative teaching strategies and mentoring. As a Program Director, the successful candidate will be able to contribute to the university’s strategic initiatives including empowering academic success, cultivating a community of learners, leading through innovation, designing distinctive experiences, redefining health and human potential, and extending our partnership. About the School: The Quinnipiac University School of Nursing has been educating nurses for more than 50 years. Our mission is to develop exceptional, practice-ready nurses as leaders in science-based, holistic care through innovation and inclusive education. The School of Nursing’s strategic priorities are aligned with innovative programs, student success, thriving community, and sustainable resources. The School of Nursing serves approximately 1100 graduate and undergraduate students. We offer CCNE accredited programs leading to BSN, MSN, and DNP degrees that prepare graduates for successful careers in hospitals, clinics, schools, communities, and many other settings. School of Nursing graduates become leaders at each level of their careers and facilitate positive changes within healthcare. Faculty and staff work with colleagues in our Center for Medicine, Nursing and Health Sciences and all schools across campus to create innovative interprofessional educational experiences that prepare students for today's health care challenges. The Center is located at our North Haven, CT campus and encompasses 325,000 square feet designed for collaborative learning including 48 pro-section stations, 16 standardized patient rooms, an exceptional health sciences library, 7 high-fidelity simulation rooms including 2 ORs and a PACU, health assessment and skills labs, advanced diagnostic imaging equipment and classrooms outfitted with the latest technology. As one of 17 schools in the nation with holistically endorsed programs, we emphasize the social, emotional, spiritual, and psychological aspects of care, as well as the physical, throughout our nursing curriculum. We are a highly collaborative and supportive community that is committed to high quality educational experience, advancing diversity in all areas. Successful candidates will share the School of Nursing values of belonging, compassion, collaboration, curiosity, and integrity. The School provides faculty members with: • A structured orientation and mentoring • An assigned faculty affiliate •Regular workshops by Quinnipiac Innovations in Learning and Teaching (QILT) • Opportunities to work with nationally recognized faculty and staff • Generous support for conference attendance and professional development • Support with grant applications for faculty research or curricular innovations • A culture of community, teamwork, and professionalism • A climate that values diversity and inclusion • Values of belonging, collaboration, compassion, curiosity and integrity The Program Director is afforded one day a week as a practice day. Although the program is online (with in person immersions), regular presence is expected on the campus in North Haven. To find out more about our School of Nursing, please visit https://www.qu.edu/schools/nursing.html About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Education, Computing & Engineering, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing, and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 21 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting multiple conference titles. This includes a 2023 NCAA National Championship win in ice hockey, a three-time defending national champion women's rugby team, and a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and just opened a South Quad with three new buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, we remain guided by the core values that define our community and shape the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: • Teaching intensive, clinical track nursing faculty position, with primary responsibility for educating graduate nursing students in the online PMHNP MSN program • Collaborate with colleagues to ensure high quality programs that demonstrate academic excellence and success • Ensure program compliance with accreditation standards • Oversee daily management of the PMHNP MSN program • Develop, maintain, and evaluate quality clinical experiences for students • Participate in student recruitment, admissions review, enrollment management, and retention initiatives to support program growth and sustainability • Design and implement learning experiences that reflect competency-based education principles • Participate in competency-based curriculum development, assessment, and continuous quality improvement aligned with the AACN 2021 Essentials • Advise and mentor students to support academic success and professional growth • Contribute to School and University service, including committee participation and professional engagement within the community • Engage in scholarly activities and maintain currency in nursing practice and education • Participate in faculty development • Engage in the School of Nursing’s strategic plan • Actively participate in the School of Nursing community Education Requirements: • Required doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DNP) in nursing or related field Qualifications: • Required unencumbered APRN license in Connecticut • Required national certification as a Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner • Recent clinical practice experience as a PMHNP • Experience with competency-based education and curriculum development • Evidence of effective teaching • Preferred experience leading or coordinating an advanced practice nursing education program, including curriculum oversight, program evaluation, accreditation activities, and faculty collaboration • Service to profession or community • Commitment to contribute to the excellence of the academic community Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically and include a resume, a cover letter detailing how your experience aligns with the position requirements, demonstrated commitment to intentional leadership that values individuals of all backgrounds and experiences, and contact information for three references. We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes tuition remission and a culture that is inclusive and driven by excellence. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful community. Advertised: September 09, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497278/clinical-assistant-professor-clinical-director-of-radiologic-science-12month": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science (12-month)",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science (12-month) Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497278 Type: Full-time Campus: North Haven - North Haven, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: Quinnipiac University's School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, open-rank, Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science at the Department of Diagnostic Imaging. This is a 12-month, year-round appointment that provides leadership and oversight of the clinical education component of the program, ensuring high-quality students’ clinical experiences, establishing, and maintaining strong clinical partnerships, student achievement of clinical competencies, and ongoing compliance with accreditation standards. This is an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful difference in the lives of future healthcare professionals while working in a collaborative and dynamic university environment. Application review will start immediately until the position is filled. About the School/Program: The School of Health Sciences is home to approximately 100 full-time faculty and staff and enrolls over 2,500 students across 30 graduate and undergraduate academic programs. The school is organized into seven departments offering undergraduate majors in biomedical sciences, diagnostic medical sonography, exercise science, health science studies, medical microbiology & immunology and radiologic sciences, and graduate programs in advanced medical imagining & leadership, biomedical sciences, cardiovascular perfusion, occupational therapy, pathologists’ assistant, physician assistant, physical therapy and social work. The school also offers entry-level dual-degrees for occupational therapy, physician assistant and physical therapy. Our school provides excellence in education, scholarship, and community engagement with a mission grounded in our commitment to producing skilled and compassionate graduates, pioneering research and partnering with our communities to advance the health and well-being of all individuals. Through unique and distinctive academic programs, interdisciplinary collaboration, immersive learning experiences, and student-centeredness, we empower students to deliver compassionate care, create innovation through research, and catalyze change in dynamic health fields. Our emphasis on evidence-based medicine, critical thinking, and interprofessional healthcare skills equips our graduates to make impactful and inclusive contributions to their professions. In all our endeavors, we are guided by a commitment to innovation, accountability, excellence, and social responsibility as we aspire to be a first-choice school of excellence and a global leader in fostering new knowledge, improving healthcare, and increasing health equity. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 22 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles — including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men’s ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: Support mission, vision, core values, and strategic plans of Quinnipiac University, and the School of Health Sciences. Coordinate the clinical education component of the Radiologic Sciences Program in collaboration with the Program Director, and in compliance with JRCERT accreditation requirements. Ensure integration of clinical education with didactic and laboratory instruction. Develop, implement, and evaluate clinical education policies, procedures, competencies, and assessment processes. Serve as the primary liaison between the program and clinical education sites. Coordinate student clinical assignments, rotations, and scheduling. Conduct clinical site visits and evaluate educational quality. Monitor student clinical performance, competency attainment, and professional behaviors. Maintain accurate clinical education records and competency documentation. Assist with clinical instructor orientation, training, and evaluation. Support JRCERT accreditation activities and outcomes assessment. Teach assigned didactic, laboratory, and/or clinical courses. Support student success, retention, and on-time graduation through participation in advising, recruitment, retention, service, department, school and institutional events. Perform additional responsibilities as assigned by the Department Chair. Education Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Radiologic Science or related field from an accredited institution. Current ARRT certification and registration in Radiography. Eligibility for Connecticut licensure. Minimum of two years of full-time clinical radiography experience. Minimum of one year of teaching experience in a JRCERT-accredited radiography program or equivalent clinical instruction experience. Knowledge of clinical education, competency-based assessment, and accreditation standards. Strong organizational, communication, and collaborative skills. Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in TED field from an accredited institution Prior experience as a Clinical Coordinator or Director of Clinical Education ARRT post-primary credential(s) Experience with JRCERT accreditation and outcomes assessment Experience with distance, hybrid, or alternative instructional modalities Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically and include a resume, a cover letter detailing how your experience aligns with the position requirements, demonstrated commitment to intentional leadership that values individuals of all backgrounds and experiences, and contact information for three references. We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes tuition remission and a culture that is inclusive and driven by excellence. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful community. Advertised: September 02, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497277/fulltime-faculty-health-and-exercise-science-nutrition": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty: Health and Exercise Science (Nutrition)",
      "description": "Full-Time Faculty: Health and Exercise Science (Nutrition) Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497277 Type: Full-time Campus: Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: Quinnipiac University’s Department of Health and Exercise Science, within the School of Health Sciences, invites applications for a full-time, 12-month faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track or Clinical Track) in the area of human nutrition. The ideal candidate is an educator who will be integral in teaching our nutrition courses and further develop the current programs that emphasize the vital role of food and nutrition in maintaining healthy lifestyles, athletic performance, medical nutrition therapy, and promoting community wellness. The successful applicant will aid our pursuit of organizing a shared learning community and contribute to the education of students in the challenges of understanding nutrition, exercise, health and wellness, population health, health equity, and public health; developing and building a strong culture of health and wellness among faculty, students, and staff; foster a student-centered environment by delivering engaging and innovative coursework; being accessible, approachable, and relatable to students; display passion, energy, and excitement in health and exercise sciences for our students; be an innovative educator who can excel in the traditional classroom and laboratory settings, with occasional hybrid or online modalities at the undergraduate level when needed; be able to participate in interdisciplinary collaboration that engage and educate students who plan to provide direct patient/client care and in public health. This is an on-ground position. The search committee will start reviewing applications immediately, and the expected start date will be in January 2027. About the School/Program: The School of Health Sciences is home to approximately 100 full-time faculty and professional staff and enrolls over 2120 students across over 22 graduate and undergraduate academic offerings. The school is organized into 7 departments offering undergraduate majors in biomedical sciences, health sciences, radiologic sciences, medical microbiology & Immunology and diagnostic medical sonography and graduate majors in physician assistant studies, occupational therapy, physical therapy, social work, biomedical sciences, pathologists’ assistant and cardiovascular perfusion. Our school provides excellence in education, scholarship, and community engagement with a mission grounded in our commitment to producing skilled and compassionate graduates, creating pioneering research, and partnering with our communities to advance the health and well-being of people and communities. Through unique and distinctive academic programs, interdisciplinary collaboration, immersive learning experiences, and student-centeredness that we empower students to deliver compassionate care, create innovation through research, and catalyze change in dynamic health fields. Our emphasis on evidence-based medicine, critical thinking, and interprofessional skills equips our graduates to make impactful and inclusive contributions to their professions. In all our endeavors, we are guided by a commitment to innovation, accountability, excellence, and social responsibility as we aspire to be a first-choice school of excellence and a global leader in fostering new knowledge, improving healthcare, and increasing health equity. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 22 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles - including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men's ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: Support the mission, vision, values, and strategic goals of Quinnipiac University and the School of Health Sciences, and the Department of Health and Exercise Science Teach classes assigned by department chair Support curriculum development and evaluation Serve as an academic advisor and mentor to students Participate in faculty development activities Participate in professional activities within and beyond School of Health Science to maximize student learning, faculty scholarship, and programmatic effectiveness Participate in student recruitment and retention activities Collaborate with faculty colleagues in teaching and research Support experiential learning and community engagement initiatives Contribute to curriculum development and innovation Support the School of Health Science and University’s vision, mission, core values and work to implement our strategic plans Provide service to the Department, SHS, QU, and the community Actively participate in the School of Health Science community In Addition, for Tenure-Track Appointment : Maintain an active research agenda, external grant applications and outputs with publications in high-quality journals in the discipline. Education Requirements: Required: Clinical Track: Master's degree (M.S. or M.P.H.) in dietetics, clinical nutrition, food and nutrition, or a related field. Tenure-Track: Doctor of Clinical Nutrition (DCN) or Ph.D. in Nutrition, or a closely related field. Preferred: Doctor of Clinical Nutrition (DCN), Ph.D. in Nutrition, post-professional or research doctoral degree in closely related field awarded by an institution accredited by a regional accrediting agency, which recognized by the U.S. Department of Education. Tenure-Track: Post-Doctorate experience and track record of external grant applications and/or awards. Qualifications: Required: Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) Independent teaching experience at the undergraduate level. Evidence of strong teaching skills and the use of instructional technology. Professional working experience in nutrition & dietetics. Commitment to community engagement and professional advocacy through teaching, service, and scholarship. For tenure track: Evidence of ability to establish a scholarly agenda (e.g., scholarship of application, discovery, integration, or teaching) through peer-reviewed publication, presentations, and ongoing research outputs and external grant applications. Preferred: Commission on Dietetic Registration (CDR) certificated specialization. At least 2 years of clinical experience in nutrition. Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically by including cover letter detailing your experience aligns with the position requirements, describing your interest in and qualifications for the role, including but not limited to your teaching, clinical experience, research, and external grant applications; curriculum vitae; teaching philosophy statement, addressing how to engage students from across academic programs (within and beyond Quinnipiac University School of Health Sciences), and ideas on integrating experiential learning into your teaching; Contact information for three professional references (on the application form). For Tenure-Track: Research agenda, published manuscripts or other evidence of scholarly outputs. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful community. Advertised: September 02, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497325/fulltime-tenure-track-faculty-finance-assistant-professor": {
      "title": "Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Assistant Professor)",
      "description": "Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Assistant Professor) Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497325 Type: Full-time Campus: Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: The School of Business at Quinnipiac University invites dynamic, innovative, and student-focused educators to join our Finance Department as a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Finance beginning in Fall 2027. We seek candidates whose research and teaching interests contribute to the evolving intersection of Finance, Financial Analytics, Artificial Intelligence, FinTech, Healthcare Finance, Biotechnology, and data-driven decision making. We welcome candidates employing both traditional and emerging approaches to important questions in finance. Opportunities exist for interdisciplinary collaboration with faculty across the School of Business and the broader university in areas related to analytics, artificial intelligence, technology, law, healthcare, and innovation. Teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate and graduate courses in finance, including Investments, Portfolio Management, Corporate Finance, Financial Markets and Institutions, Financial Analytics, FinTech, Decentralized Finance (DeFi), and related areas. The successful candidate will have opportunities to contribute to the continued development of innovative programs in Financial Technology, Financial Analytics, and AI applications in finance as well as university initiatives in Healthcare Finance. Candidates should demonstrate the potential to establish and sustain a high-impact research agenda that contributes to leading finance journals. The department is particularly interested in candidates whose scholarship explores how emerging technologies are reshaping financial markets, institutions, firms, and investors. Relevant areas may include, but are not limited to: Artificial intelligence and machine learning in financial decision-making Asset pricing Investment analysis Portfolio management Financial analytics and predictive modeling Alternative data and computational finance FinTech innovation Digital assets, blockchain, and decentralized finance Generative AI and large language models in finance AI governance, regulation, and the ethical implications for financial markets The successful candidate will play a central role in a premier finance program focused on preparing graduates for careers in a rapidly changing financial landscape. Faculty joining the department at this pivotal moment will have the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to program innovation, curriculum development, and the future direction of finance education at Quinnipiac. About the School: At the Quinnipiac University School of Business, we holistically educate and equip learners for meaningful lives and careers in dynamic, interdependent global environments. We advance this mission through excellence in teaching, research, and experiential learning, while fostering an inclusive academic community that emphasizes critical thinking, ethical leadership, innovation, and the uniquely human qualities that enable graduates to make a positive impact in their professions and communities. Faculty are supported in pursuing excellence in both teaching and research and are encouraged to explore new ideas, develop innovative pedagogies, and contribute to an inclusive learning environment that helps students achieve their full potential. Through teaching and research mentors and both internal and external professional development opportunities, new faculty are equipped with the tools they need to succeed in a higher education environment. The School of Business is a thriving, student-centered community that serves approximately 1,450 undergraduate students and 550 graduate students. We offer 13 undergraduate majors, 15 minors, 3 dual-degree programs, 4 accelerated dual-degree programs, and 5 graduate degree programs, delivered through both in-person and online formats. The school is AACSB accredited in business and holds the distinctive AACSB accreditation in accounting. Our success is reflected in our 99% placement rate among undergraduate and graduate students. Our community includes 60 full-time faculty members, administrators, and professional staff who share a commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and service. As a signatory to the United Nations Principles for Responsible Management Education (UNPRME), we seek to prepare students to make meaningful contributions to organizations and society. This is an especially exciting time to join the School of Business. As part of the university's vision for the future, Quinnipiac has invested in a new state-of-the-art academic facility, opened in Fall 2025, that is designed to enhance student learning, collaboration, and community while providing faculty with exceptional spaces for research, innovative pedagogy, and immersive learning experiences. https://www.qu.edu/quinnipiac-today/building-the-university-of-the-future/ Quinnipiac School of Business faculty also benefit from a wide range of resources that support both scholarship and teaching, including the User Experience & Behavioral Insights Lab, the Financial Technology Center, Analytics & Applied AI Lab, Content Creation Studio, and the Sales Center. The school is home to two nationally recognized centers, the M&T Bank Center for Women and Business and the M&T Bank Center for Innovation and Entrepreneurship, which provide unique opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration, research, community engagement, and applied learning. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 22 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles — including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men’s ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and graduate finance courses, both online and on ground Maintain an active research agenda leading to publication in high-quality journals Advise and mentor students Actively participate in department, school, and university service Collaborate with faculty colleagues in teaching and research Support experiential learning and industry engagement initiatives Contribute to curriculum development and program innovation Assist with recruitment, retention, and co-curricular activities Help build external partnerships that support teaching, research, and student success Support the University’s Lifelong Learning Initiatives Education Requirements: Ph.D. in Finance, FinTech, Economics, or a closely related field from an accredited Business School or University. ABD candidates must have all degree requirements completed prior to the start date Qualifications: Primary Qualifications Ph.D. in Finance, Economics, or closely related field from an accredited institution Demonstrated excellence in teaching Ability to engage students in active and experiential learning Scholarly activity sufficient to meet Quinnipiac University School of Business AACSB Scholarly Academic standards Demonstrated ability to contribute positively to a collaborative academic environment Preferred Qualifications Experience using programming, statistical, or analytical tools such as Python, R, SQL, machine learning frameworks, or related technologies Prior teaching experience in Financial Analytics, FinTech, or AI-related finance courses. Evidence of interdisciplinary collaboration involving technology and finance. Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically and include a resume, a cover letter detailing how your experience aligns with the position requirements, demonstrated commitment to intentional leadership that values individuals of all backgrounds and experiences, and contact information for three references. In addition, please submit as part of your application: • A curriculum vitae (please include evidence of teaching effectiveness, relevant industry experience, student mentoring, scholarly activity, and service) • A description of previous teaching experience including course evaluations • Research manuscript, paper, or other evidence of scholarly engagement We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes tuition remission and a culture that is inclusive and driven by excellence. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful community. Advertised: August 25, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497326/fulltime-tenure-track-faculty-finance-associate-professor": {
      "title": "Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Associate Professor)",
      "description": "Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Associate Professor) Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497326 Type: Full-time Campus: Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: The School of Business at Quinnipiac University invites dynamic, innovative, and student-focused educators to join our Finance Department as a tenure-track Associate Professor of Finance beginning in Fall 2027. The School of Business seeks a faculty member who can contribute not only through excellence in teaching and scholarship, but also through leadership in program development, faculty collaboration, industry engagement, and strategic initiatives. The successful candidate will help shape the future direction of finance education, contribute to strategic initiatives across the School of Business, and play a meaningful role in the continued growth of the department's nationally recognized finance and financial technology programs. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a record of academic accomplishment and evidence of leadership potential in areas such as curriculum development, program administration, faculty governance, industry engagement, junior faculty mentoring, student mentoring, and strategic initiatives. We seek candidates whose research and teaching interests contribute to the evolving intersection of Finance, Financial Analytics, Artificial Intelligence, FinTech, Healthcare Finance, Biotechnology, and data-driven decision making. We welcome candidates employing both traditional and emerging approaches to important questions in finance. Opportunities exist for interdisciplinary collaboration with faculty across the School of Business and the broader university in areas related to analytics, artificial intelligence, technology, law, healthcare, and innovation. Teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate and graduate courses in finance, including Investments, Portfolio Management, Corporate Finance, Financial Markets and Institutions, Financial Analytics, FinTech, Decentralized Finance (DeFi), and related areas. The successful candidate will have opportunities to contribute to the continued development of innovative programs in Financial Technology, Financial Analytics, Healthcare Finance, and AI applications in finance. Candidates should demonstrate an established and sustained record of scholarly achievement, with evidence of continuing contributions to high-quality finance research. The department is particularly interested in candidates whose scholarship explores how emerging technologies are reshaping financial markets, institutions, firms, and investors. Relevant areas may include, but are not limited to: Artificial intelligence and machine learning in financial decision-making Asset pricing Investment analysis Portfolio management Financial analytics and predictive modeling Alternative data and computational finance FinTech innovation Digital assets, blockchain, and decentralized finance Generative AI and large language models in finance AI governance, regulation, and the ethical implications for financial markets About the School: At the Quinnipiac University School of Business, we holistically educate and equip learners for meaningful lives and careers in dynamic, interdependent global environments. We advance this mission through excellence in teaching, research, and experiential learning, while fostering an inclusive academic community that emphasizes critical thinking, ethical leadership, innovation, and the uniquely human qualities that enable graduates to make a positive impact in their professions and communities. Faculty are supported in pursuing excellence in both teaching and research and are encouraged to explore new ideas, develop innovative pedagogies, and contribute to an inclusive learning environment that helps students achieve their full potential. Through teaching and research mentors and both internal and external professional development opportunities, new faculty are equipped with the tools they need to succeed in a higher education environment. The School of Business is a thriving, student-centered community that serves approximately 1,450 undergraduate students and 550 graduate students. We offer 13 undergraduate majors, 15 minors, 3 dual-degree programs, 4 accelerated dual-degree programs, and 5 graduate degree programs, delivered through both in-person and online formats. The school is AACSB accredited in business and holds the distinctive AACSB accreditation in accounting. Our success is reflected in our 99% placement rate among undergraduate and graduate students. Our community includes 60 full-time faculty members, administrators, and professional staff who share a commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and service. As a signatory to the United Nations Principles for Responsible Management Education (UNPRME), we seek to prepare students to make meaningful contributions to organizations and society. This is an especially exciting time to join the School of Business. As part of the university's vision for the future, Quinnipiac has invested in a new state-of-the-art academic facility, opened in Fall 2025, that is designed to enhance student learning, collaboration, and community while providing faculty with exceptional spaces for research, innovative pedagogy, and immersive learning experiences. https://www.qu.edu/quinnipiac-today/building-the-university-of-the-future/ Quinnipiac School of Business faculty also benefit from a wide range of resources that support both scholarship and teaching, including the User Experience & Behavioral Insights Lab, Financial Technology Center, Analytics & Applied AI Lab, Content Creation Studio, and the Sales Center. The school is home to two nationally recognized centers, the M&T Bank Center for Women and Business and the M&T Bank Center for Innovation and Entrepreneurship, which provide unique opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration, research, community engagement, and applied learning. About the Department The Finance Department offers a collaborative and intellectually vibrant environment where faculty are committed to excellence in both teaching and scholarship. As the largest major in the School of Business, the department offers both a B.S. in Finance and a B.S. in Financial Technology. Faculty also contribute to graduate education through the MBA and Professional MBA programs. What truly distinguishes the Quinnipiac finance experience is the opportunity to connect classroom learning with industry engagement at the highest levels. The department oversees the Quinnipiac University Global Asset Management Education Forum (GAME), the largest student-run finance conference in the world. Each year, GAME brings together nearly 1,500 students and faculty from more than 125 global colleges and universities, creating unparalleled opportunities for faculty and students to engage with and learn from renowned leaders across the financial industry. Faculty and students also benefit from access to our state-of-the-art Financial Technology Center, which supports experiential learning and serves as the home of the department’s $6.0 million student-managed investment fund. Together, these programs create a rich environment where faculty can mentor students, pursue innovative ideas, and connect academic learning with professional practice. Faculty maintain active research agendas and publish in leading journals in finance, economics, and related disciplines. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 20 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles — including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men’s ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: Primary Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate finance courses, both online and on ground Maintain an active research agenda leading to publication in high-quality journals Advise and mentor students Actively participate in department, school, and university service Collaborate with faculty colleagues in teaching and research Support experiential learning and industry engagement initiatives Contribute to curriculum development and program innovation Assist with recruitment, retention, and co-curricular activities Help build external partnerships that support teaching, research, and student success Support the University’s Lifelong Learning Initiatives Additional Responsibilities May Include Providing leadership in curriculum development and assessment initiatives Supporting strategic planning efforts within the department and School of Business Mentoring junior faculty and contributing to faculty development initiatives Assisting with accreditation, program review, and assessment activities Helping strengthen relationships with industry partners, alumni, and professional organizations Education Requirements: Ph.D. in Finance, FinTech, Economics, or a closely related field from an accredited Business School or University Qualifications: Primary Qualifications Ph.D. in Finance, Economics, or closely related field from an accredited institution Demonstrated excellence in teaching Ability to engage students in active and experiential learning Scholarly activity sufficient to meet Quinnipiac University School of Business AACSB Scholarly Academic standards Demonstrated ability to contribute positively to a collaborative academic environment Demonstrated experience leading academic, professional, or strategic initiatives Experience with curriculum development, assessment, or program innovation Experience building partnerships with industry, alumni, or external stakeholders Experience mentoring junior faculty and students Evidence of successful collaboration across departments or disciplines Interest in future leadership opportunities within the department, school, or university Preferred Qualifications Experience using programming, statistical, or analytical tools such as Python, R, SQL, machine learning frameworks, or related technologies Prior experience teaching experience in Financial Analytics, FinTech, or AI-related finance courses. Evidence of interdisciplinary collaboration involving technology and finance. Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically and include a resume, a cover letter detailing how your experience aligns with the position requirements, demonstrated commitment to intentional leadership that values individuals of all backgrounds and experiences, and contact information for three references. In addition, please submit as part of your application: • A curriculum vitae (please include evidence of teaching effectiveness, relevant industry experience, student mentoring, scholarly activity, and service) • A description of previous teaching experience including course evaluations • Research manuscript, paper, or other evidence of scholarly engagement • Evidence of leadership roles We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes tuition remission and a culture that is inclusive and driven by excellence. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful community. Advertised: August 25, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
